**Read:** [Convective Heat Transfer — Arup Kumar Das](../sources/Convective-Heat-Transfer-Das.lingua#r_1BYB2QY61ENBK9WGCHBBC5YE92), the complete four-week course; [Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF), the full convection and instability progression; [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), complete applicable convection chapters; [Convecção e métodos numéricos — Maliska, UFSC](../sources/Conveccao-and-Numerical-Methods-Maliska-UFSC.lingua#r_71K7JMRA8M0N3Y8EKMZJT9NGQ7), available complete convection course.

Complete the NPTEL convective sequence and the relevant full analytical heat-transfer lectures. Derive a boundary-layer or internal-flow solution, stating the ordering arguments and boundary conditions. Compare imposed wall temperature with imposed wall heat flux and distinguish local from average results.

Investigate one forced and one buoyancy-driven configuration over documented parameter ranges. Test correlation selection, property evaluation, developing-flow effects and uncertainty. Where transition or turbulence enters, identify the closure and the evidence supporting it instead of extrapolating a laminar result.

Deliver derivations, dimensionless maps, energy/pressure accounts and a comparison with a complete published experiment or performed measurement. Include pumping or ventilation cost and evaluate a changed geometry. Explain which disagreement arises from implementation, uncertain conditions or an inappropriate physical approximation.

**Continue:** [A complete thermal service from physics to continuing use](A-complete-thermal-service-from-physics-to-continuing-use.lingua#r_7J8HFJ2KFHGSRF5EB4JFNRZRB2).

